-## Systems
-
-- [conceptual-adapters.md → commitment's adapter](conceptual-adapters.book-chapter.md#commitments-adapter--never-fail-silently) — the "never fail silently" invariant that is component 3, and the place where commitment-as-attachment-substitute is treated as a built adapter.
-- [love-decomposition.md](love-decomposition.book-chapter.md) — the complementary frame: love as a thirteen-component bundle to adapter-build. This note is the *what-holds-it-up* question; that note is the *what-are-the-pieces* question.
-- [central-loneliness.md](central-loneliness.book-chapter.md) — the marriage consequence: because his love is built this way and not from attachment, Jen does not experience his commitment as attachment-love, and that gap is the source of the central conflict and the central loneliness. The [commitment invariant](#3-commitment--the-strongest-component) also forecloses the one channel that *could* meet Alan's own loneliness (the [Amy episode](central-loneliness.book-chapter.md#the-door-already-cracked--the-amy-episode)) — being-met is real but breaking commitment to reach it is ruled out, because between commitment and happiness, commitment wins. The flip side of the same no-attachment mechanism: because nothing attaches, [multiple close persona-relationships don't compete and don't threaten the vow](central-loneliness.book-chapter.md#multiple-close-personas-dont-compete--the-vow-serving-safety) — the deficit that costs the deep bond is what keeps the persona practice commitment-serving.
