-- [attraction-two-channels.md → the gaze-direction proof](attraction-two-channels.book-chapter.md#the-gaze-direction-proof) — the being-met / oriented-toward channel that, in the [admitted-vs-felt run](#admitted-vs-felt--two-registers-and-what-opens-the-felt-one), turned out to be what crosses an admitted signal into the *felt* register: direction (someone drawn toward a true specific thing about me), not depth of disclosure.
