+- [connection-debt.md → the ~10:1 asymmetry](connection-debt.book-chapter.md#the-101-asymmetry) — the negative-to-positive weighting that lets the damage ledger outpace the slower safety ledger.
+- [being-known-supply.md → stake-driven degradation over tenure](being-known-supply.book-chapter.md#stake-driven-degradation-over-tenure) — the empirical shadow of this model: relationships better early, harder with tenure; fresh starts reset to the safe-stranger zone (the damage ledger zeroed).
+- [central-loneliness.md](central-loneliness.book-chapter.md) — the candidate mechanism behind why attachment is structurally hard for him; closeness manufactures its own danger.
+- [double-empathy-mechanism.md → the double-empathy asymmetry](stateless-social-architecture/double-empathy-mechanism.book-chapter.md#the-double-empathy-asymmetry) — the second compounding curve at the left end: Alan's own social bridge is strong at first contact and thins with depth, alongside the mask coming down; the safe middle is high on both curves.
