+- [being-known-cost.md → why Jen's cost runs doubly high](being-known-cost.book-chapter.md#why-jens-cost-runs-doubly-high--hyperfantasia) — the imagery-axis polarity (Alan's aphantasia ↔ Jen's hyperfantasia) underneath the memory asymmetry: her state-dependent reconstruction is the same vivid-emotional-memory trait, seen from the dispute side.
+- [action-epistemology.md](action-epistemology.book-chapter.md) — the valuing-Truth drive that makes Alan prefer the painful accurate record over the comfortable one, and that he suspects Jen's architecture, unlike his, can decline.
