+- [alexithymia.md → the missing narrative substrate](alexithymia.book-chapter.md#the-precise-locus--the-missing-narrative-substrate) — the missing track the feeling would have accrued on; why the markers kept intensity and lost content.
+- [mission-break.md](mission-break.book-chapter.md) — the age-20 nervous-system-break onset the felt-channel closure is proposed to coincide with; the safety collapse that is a candidate cause for the live read going dark.
+- [disputed-misery.md → the saliency-bias rebuttal](disputed-misery.book-chapter.md#the-saliency-bias-rebuttal) — the one area (grown up in the church) where Alan self-flags his own retrospective saliency bias; the pre-20 "felt channel was open" memory sits inside that flagged zone.
+- [safety.md](safety.book-chapter.md) — the bar that gates the live read; Alan waits for it to recover so the feeling recurs and he can read it.
+- [discrete-self.md](discrete-self.book-chapter.md) / [multiversal-identity.md](multiversal-identity.book-chapter.md) — the ephemeral-self frame that makes wanting an unkeepable feeling coherent: identity itself is ephemeral, so for the Alans that get to feel, feeling is worth having while it lasts.
